Welcome to the Official Lightbox GitHub Repository!

If you have made it here, you have probably visited the website associated with this.
I would like to personally thank you for visiting it as it details a majority
of extracurricular work that I have done as an aspiring IT professional.
As you visit this repository, it is worth noting a few things:

1. BUGS AND MODIFICATIONS
Nearly all projects in this repository are subject to significant change
because there are several projects that may still have undiscovered bugs. If you
use and run any of my code and encounter any bugs, email me right away at:
stephjay442@gmail.com so that I can assess the effect the bug has on the script
and fix it within reasonable time. If you have tested one of my scripts and
find a bug in it, I will give credit to you in a list of bug hunters and
script testers that will appear on this repository in a text file.

2. DISTRIBUTION AND USE
You are free to distribute, use, and edit my work as long as you give credit 
to me as the original owner. My work is licensed under the GNU GPLv3 license,
which in itself is also free and open-source and sets out the guidelines
referring to the distribution and use of open-source code. 
This license prohibits selling such work under a proprietary license. 
Please read the GNU GPLv3 license attached to this repository, under LICENSE.

3. PROJECT ENHANCEMENT
No project in this repository may ever be truly finished.
This mostly links back to the first point, except additional features
may be added to any given project in the near future to enhance
user experience and improve overall functionality and versatility.

4. ADDITIONAL DOCUMENTATION
In the event that this repository becomes too large,
current and future content may disappear from immediate view 
and be nested in various directories. While this is unlikely,
documentation for each single project is a planned part of this
repository that will serve as an introductory manual to the 
tool that it concerns. In this case, directories containing
both the relevant code and documentation will be made available
as opposed to plain .cpp or .py files appearing unorganized.

5. NOTICE OF RESPONSIBLE USE AND SAFETY
Use my tools responsibly and professionally. Some of the 
tools made available on this repository are capable of supporting
both security analyst tasks and cyber attacking tasks.
Such programs that have been evaluated to be potentially
used in such manners have been modified to include a security
disclaimer at the top of the terminal window upon execution.
Do not use any tools that I have created in order to support
missions in digital attacks on a scale ranging from the personal
level to the enterprise level. Such activities are 
punishable by State and Federal Law.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thank you for stopping by! I hope you find the following information
valuable and helpful. Do not hesitate to contact me with any
issues you encounter when visiting this repository or using my code.
